IMPORT prelude

-- Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 (Singapore) -- what an LLP is, who may be a partner, the partners'
-- limited liability, a partner's power to bind, leaving, bankruptcy, assignment, the two-partner minimum, the
-- manager, publication, and the bar on bankrupt managers: ss 4 to 17, 28, 29, 33 and 58.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ (amendments to Act 21 of 2024 and Act 30 of 2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 115 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, second only to the Companies
-- Act. Most of those citations are to s 2 (92 Acts) and s 4 (19): other Acts pull LLPs into their definition of a
-- body corporate. SCOPED: Part 2, the two-partner and manager rules, and the First Schedule's default terms. Not
-- encoded: registration and names (Part 3), conversion (Part 4) except the Second Schedule's partner-liability rule,
-- accounts and filings, receivership and winding up, the register of controllers (Part 6A), striking off, and the
-- offences machinery.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 -- nature and partners`

§§ `4, 10 -- a body corporate, outside partnership law`

-- s 4(1): an LLP "is a body corporate which is formed by being registered under this Act and which has legal
-- personality separate from that of its partners". (3): "Any change in the partners ... does not affect the existence,
-- rights or liabilities". s 10: "Except as otherwise provided by this Act, the law relating to partnerships does not
-- apply to a limited liability partnership."
GIVEN `registered under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the business is a limited liability partnership` IF
    `registered under the Act`

GIVEN `a partner has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change affects the LLP's existence, rights or liabilities` IF
    FALSE

§§ `11 -- who may be a partner`

-- s 11(1): "Any individual or body corporate may be a partner". (2): "body corporate excludes any trade union or
-- platform work association". (A firm, which is not a body corporate, cannot be a partner.)
DECLARE PartnerKind IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company`
    `another LLP`
    `a foreign company`
    `a registered trade union`
    `a platform work association`
    `an unincorporated firm`
    `an unincorporated society`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A PartnerKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be a partner` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another LLP` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a foreign company` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7, 8 -- deeds without a seal`

-- s 7(1): a deed may be executed without a seal by signature "(a) ... by at least 2 partners ...; or (b) ... by a
-- partner ... in the presence of a witness who attests the signature." (3): a person signing for more than one LLP
-- must sign "separately in each capacity". s 6(1): an LLP "may have a common seal but need not have one".
DECLARE DeedExecution HAS
    `the number of partners who signed` IS A NUMBER
    `a witness attested a partner's signature` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the signatory signs for more than one LLP` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed separately in each capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the common seal was affixed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the execution` IS A DeedExecution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deed is validly executed without a seal` IF
        (    `the execution`'s `the number of partners who signed` AT LEAST 2
         OR  (    `the execution`'s `the number of partners who signed` AT LEAST 1
              AND `the execution`'s `a witness attested a partner's signature`))
    AND (    NOT `the execution`'s `the signatory signs for more than one LLP`
         OR  `the execution`'s `signed separately in each capacity`)

GIVEN `the execution` IS A DeedExecution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deed binds as a deed` IF
        `the deed is validly executed without a seal` `the execution`
    OR  `the execution`'s `the common seal was affixed`

§§ `12 -- limited liability`

-- s 12(1): "An obligation of the limited liability partnership, whether arising in contract, tort or otherwise, is
-- solely the obligation of the limited liability partnership."
-- (2): a partner is not personally liable for it "solely by reason of being a partner".
-- (3): this does not affect "the personal liability of a partner IN TORT for the partner's OWN wrongful act or
-- omission, but a partner is not personally liable for the wrongful act or omission of any OTHER partner".
-- (4): where a partner is liable to a person (OTHER THAN another partner) for a wrongful act in the course of the
-- LLP's business or with its authority, "the limited liability partnership is liable to the same extent".
--
-- The carve-out in (3) is for TORT. A partner who personally breaches a contract the LLP made is not liable on it:
-- the contract is the LLP's obligation. And (4) does not run in favour of a fellow partner: a partner harmed by
-- another partner's wrong in the course of business cannot use (4) to make the LLP liable.
DECLARE Wrong IS ONE OF
    `the partner's own tort`
    `another partner's tort`
    `the LLP's contract`
    `the LLP's debt`

GIVEN `the wrong` IS A Wrong, `the partner gave a personal guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the partner is personally liable` IF
    CONSIDER `the wrong`
    WHEN `the partner's own tort` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another partner's tort` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `the partner gave a personal guarantee`

DECLARE TortClaim HAS
    `the partner is liable for their own wrongful act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the course of the LLP's business or with its authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is another partner` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claim` IS A TortClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the LLP is liable to the same extent as the partner` IF
        `the claim`'s `the partner is liable for their own wrongful act`
    AND `the claim`'s `in the course of the LLP's business or with its authority`
    AND NOT `the claim`'s `the claimant is another partner`

§§ `13 -- a partner's power to bind`

-- s 13(1): "Every partner ... is the agent of the limited liability partnership."
-- (2): the LLP "is not bound by anything done by a partner in dealing with a person if -- (a) the partner has in fact
-- no authority ...; AND (b) the person KNOWS that the partner has no authority OR does NOT KNOW OR BELIEVE the partner
-- to be a partner".
-- (3): a former partner is "regarded (in relation to any person dealing with the [LLP]) as still being a partner ...
-- unless -- (a) the person has notice that the former partner has ceased ...; or (b) notice ... has been delivered to
-- the Registrar."
--
-- So an unauthorised partner still binds the LLP in dealing with someone who believes them a partner and does not
-- know of the lack of authority. And the LLP escapes a former partner's dealings by filing with the Registrar,
-- whether or not the person dealing ever looked.
DECLARE Dealing HAS
    `the partner had actual authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person knew the partner lacked authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person knew or believed the partner to be a partner` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the LLP is bound by the partner's act` IF
        `the dealing`'s `the partner had actual authority`
    OR  (    NOT `the dealing`'s `the person knew the partner lacked authority`
         AND `the dealing`'s `the person knew or believed the partner to be a partner`)

DECLARE FormerPartner HAS
    `the person dealing had notice of the cessation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice of the cessation was delivered to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the former` IS A FormerPartner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the former partner is still regarded as a partner` IF
        NOT `the former`'s `the person dealing had notice of the cessation`
    AND NOT `the former`'s `notice of the cessation was delivered to the Registrar`

§§ `15 -- leaving`

-- s 15(1): a partner may cease "in accordance with the limited liability partnership agreement, or in the absence of
-- such agreement, by that partner giving 30 DAYS' NOTICE". (2): death or dissolution ends it.
-- (3): unless the agreement provides otherwise, the former partner is entitled to "(a) ... capital contribution ...
-- and ... right to share in the accumulated profits ... after the deduction of losses ...; and (b) determined as at the
-- date the former partner ceased". (4): they "must not interfere in the management".
--
-- The default payout is capital plus share of accumulated profits net of losses. It does not include goodwill or the
-- value of the business as a going concern; and if losses exceed the profits, the text does not say whether the
-- shortfall comes off the capital.
DECLARE Departure HAS
    `the agreement provides for leaving` IS A BOOLEAN
    `left as the agreement provides` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of notice given` IS A NUMBER
    `died or was dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the departure` IS A Departure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the partner has ceased to be a partner` IF
        `the departure`'s `died or was dissolved`
    OR  (    `the departure`'s `the agreement provides for leaving`
         AND `the departure`'s `left as the agreement provides`)
    OR  (    NOT `the departure`'s `the agreement provides for leaving`
         AND `the departure`'s `days of notice given` AT LEAST 30)

GIVEN `capital contribution` IS A NUMBER, `share of accumulated profits` IS A NUMBER, `share of losses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the default payout to a departing partner` MEANS
    `capital contribution` PLUS `share of accumulated profits` MINUS `share of losses`

§§ `16, 17, 58 -- bankruptcy and assignment`

-- s 16: unless the agreement provides otherwise, bankruptcy "(a) ... does not by itself cause the bankrupt partner to
-- cease being a partner ..., but the restriction ... under section 58 applies; and (b) the Official Assignee ... must not
-- interfere in the management ... but is entitled to receive distributions".
-- s 58(1): an undischarged bankrupt who "acts as manager of any limited liability partnership without the permission
-- of the General Division of the High Court or the written permission of the Official Assignee" commits an offence --
-- $10,000 or 2 years.
-- s 2(1): "manager" means "any person (whether or not a partner ...) who is concerned in or takes part in the
-- management".
-- First Schedule para 4 (the default term): "Every partner may take part in the management".
--
-- Read together: under the default terms a bankrupt partner remains a partner with a right to take part in
-- management, and exercising that right makes them a "manager" who commits the s 58 offence. The default right and the
-- offence collide; only the court's or the Official Assignee's permission resolves it.
DECLARE BankruptPartner HAS
    `the agreement provides that bankruptcy ends partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `takes part in management` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the court's or the Official Assignee's permission` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the partner` IS A BankruptPartner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bankrupt remains a partner` IF
    NOT `the partner`'s `the agreement provides that bankruptcy ends partnership`

GIVEN `the partner` IS A BankruptPartner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bankrupt partner commits the section 58 offence` IF
        `the partner`'s `takes part in management`
    AND NOT `the partner`'s `has the court's or the Official Assignee's permission`

-- s 17: a partner may assign their interest "but only to the extent that the assignee becomes entitled to receive
-- distributions"; the assignment does not end the partnership or let the assignee interfere in management.
DECLARE AssigneeRight IS ONE OF
    `receiving distributions`
    `taking part in management`
    `voting`
    `becoming a partner`

GIVEN `the right` IS AN AssigneeRight
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assignee acquires the right` IF
    CONSIDER `the right`
    WHEN `receiving distributions` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `28 -- the two-partner minimum`

-- s 28(1): "at least 2 partners". (2): if it carries on business with fewer than 2 partners "for a period of more than 2
-- years", a person is personally liable jointly and severally "for any obligation ... incurred during the period that
-- the [LLP] so carries on business AFTER THOSE 2 YEARS if, at the time the obligation was incurred, the person -- (a) was
-- a partner ...; and (b) KNEW that the [LLP] was carrying on business with fewer than 2 partners for a period of more
-- than 2 years."
--
-- The sole remaining partner who does not KNOW the two years have passed keeps limited liability. The test is knowledge,
-- not constructive knowledge.
DECLARE SolePartnerDebt HAS
    `months trading with fewer than 2 partners when the debt was incurred` IS A NUMBER
    `the person was a partner when the debt was incurred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person knew it had been more than 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the debt` IS A SolePartnerDebt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the partner is personally liable for the debt under section 28` IF
        `the debt`'s `months trading with fewer than 2 partners when the debt was incurred` GREATER THAN 24
    AND `the debt`'s `the person was a partner when the debt was incurred`
    AND `the debt`'s `the person knew it had been more than 2 years`

§§ `29 -- the manager`

-- s 29(1): at least one manager who "(a) is a natural person; (b) has attained 18 years of age and is otherwise of full
-- legal capacity; and (c) is ordinarily resident in Singapore." (4): contravention -- the LLP AND EVERY PARTNER, $5,000
-- and $200 a day.
DECLARE ManagerCandidate HAS
    `is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `of full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an undischarged bankrupt without permission` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A ManagerCandidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate meets section 29(1)` IF
        `the candidate`'s `is a natural person`
    AND `the candidate`'s `age` AT LEAST 18
    AND `the candidate`'s `of full legal capacity`
    AND `the candidate`'s `ordinarily resident in Singapore`

-- s 29(1) itself does not exclude a bankrupt; s 58 makes their acting an offence. Both are needed for a lawful manager.
GIVEN `the candidate` IS A ManagerCandidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate may lawfully be the required manager` IF
        `the candidate meets section 29(1)` `the candidate`
    AND NOT `the candidate`'s `is an undischarged bankrupt without permission`

§§ `33 -- invoices and correspondence`

-- s 33(1): invoices and official correspondence must bear "(a) the name and registration number ...; (b) a statement
-- that it is registered with limited liability." (2): $1,000 and $200 a day.
GIVEN `shows name and registration number` IS A BOOLEAN, `states it is registered with limited liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the invoice complies with section 33` IF
    `shows name and registration number` AND `states it is registered with limited liability`
